-- title:
--   An element of y outside (U,varpi) at a crossing end
-- statement:
--   Setting. Let $q$ and $\ell$ be primes with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$, and let $M'$ be a non-zero natural number with $q\nmid M'$ (`hqM'`) and $\ell\mid M'$ (`hℓM'`). Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ (`hζ`), and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\zeta)=e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be, by `hH₁`, the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell)^\times$; thus $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L(\!(t)\!)$ which by `hK` is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the subfield of $L(\!(t)\!)$ generated over $L$ by the image, under coefficientwise extension of scalars from $\mathbb Q$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a Henselian discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be non-zero whose Laurent series is the image of the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for a unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C:=$ `chartAlgFin A K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin A K j` for $j$ regarded as an element of $C$. Let $y\subset C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no non-zero point killed by $q$.
--
--   Throughout, a *level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$* means an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29): for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ and $p_g$ having non-zero associated Laurent series, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the ratio of those series, and every embedding $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\zeta)=e^{2\pi i/q}$, the series $\iota(\tau x)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\delta=\begin{pmatrix}\delta_{00}&\delta_{01}/q\\ q\,\delta_{10}&\delta_{11}\end{pmatrix}$.
--
--   Rigidity hypotheses. The hypothesis `hArig` asserts, for every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $X:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout of the two affine charts of $C$ and of the $j^{-1}$-chart algebra), every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ equal to the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec}A$ (`hϖz`) and lying in $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O_{X,z}}$ (`hz`), and every point $y'$ of `XFin A K j` mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` (`hy'`) at which the supersingularity condition `hss'` holds (the analogue of `hss` for $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$), the existence of a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma\colon A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ onto $S:=W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/\big(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v-f\,u\big)$, satisfying the seven clauses listed below.
--
--   A particular such configuration is then fixed: a point $z$ with germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$, a point $y'$ of `XFin A K j` above $z$ with the supersingularity property `hss'` and with $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}=y$ (`hy'y`), a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1\colon A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1-(X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1)\in(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ onto $S:=W_1[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/\big(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1\big)$. Writing $\mathrm{toC}$ for the map from $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ to its completion, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germY}$ for the composite of the canonical identification of the global sections of the chart with $C$ and the germ map at $z$ through $y'$, the hypothesis `hW₁` states the seven clauses for this data: (1) for $a\in A$, $e_1$ carries the germ of $a$ to the class of $C(\sigma_1 a)$; (2) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$; (3) if in addition $\gamma_{11}\equiv 1\pmod\ell$, then $\tau$ acts trivially modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, i.e. $\tau a-a\in y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ for all $a\in C$; (4) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and acting trivially modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W_1$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W_1)$ such that $\theta$ is compatible with $\tau$ under $e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$, $\theta$ fixes all constants, $\theta(X_{j})\equiv\sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$ and $M\equiv c\,\gamma$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$, $c\equiv1$ whenever $\gamma_{11}\equiv1\pmod\ell$, and $c\not\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (5) for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each omitting at least one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma_1\varpi)$, and each containing an element $a_iX_0+b_iX_1+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ along $e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}$ are distinct; (6) for a prime $P$ of $S$ omitting one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, containing the class of $C(\sigma_1\varpi)$ and containing some $X_0+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a\in C$ has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$ in $L$; (7) the series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $q$-expansion of $j$ with all exponents multiplied by $q$) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0\in A$ with the difference of that element and $a_0$ in $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, an integer $e_0\ge1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a,b\in W_1$ with at least one a unit and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ the value $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}(\text{coefficient of }X_0^iX_1^{e_0-i}\text{ in }h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit, and $e_1$ carries the germ of that difference to the class of $h$.
--
--   The blown-up algebra and its valuation-theoretic data. By `hJ`, $J\subseteq C$ is the infimum of the ideals $\tau^{-1}\big((e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY})^{-1}(\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)),\mathrm{mkS}(X_0),\mathrm{mkS}(X_1))\big)$, taken over $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$. By `hB`, $B$ is the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained by adjoining to $C$ all $x\in K$ with $x\varpi_t\in J$. A valuation subring $W$ of $K$ contains $B$ (`hBW`), and: `hR1` states that $C\le B$ and that every element of $K$ is a quotient of elements of $B$ with non-zero denominator; `hR2` states that $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) states that an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b\in C$ one has $b\in y$ if and only if $b\in\mathfrak m_W$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak m_W$ in the sense that $f\in W$ iff $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h\notin\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) requires: for every $A$-compatible structure of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra on the residue field of $A$, a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) whose kernel is $B\cap\mathfrak m_W$, which induces the residue map on $A$, and which for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$ intertwines $\tau$ with [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) at an element $c\in\mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ such that $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), with $c\ne1$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; that every such $\tau$ maps $B$ into $B$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is obtained from some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ as the set of images $\tau(b)$ of elements $b\in B\cap\mathfrak m_W$; that an element of $B$ all of whose $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$-translates lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$; and that a level automorphism preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$. Furthermore `hjK` and `hjC` state that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and `m` is a natural number with $1\le m$ (`hm1`) and $\varpi^m=\varpi_t w$ for a unit $w$ (`hmt`).
--
--   Ends and the crossing chart. By `hends`, a subring $O$ of $K$ belongs to the finite set `ends` precisely when there is a non-zero $a\in J$ such that, with $B_a$ the $A$-algebra obtained by adjoining to $C$ all $x\in K$ with $xa\in J$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with $O$ the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ (that is, $f\in O$ iff $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_a$, $h\notin P$), such that every element of $y$ lying in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$, and such that $B\not\subseteq O$. Let $O\in$ `ends` (`hOmem`) with $O\subseteq W$ (`hOW`), $O$ local (`hOloc`) and Noetherian (`hOnoe`), and $C\subseteq O$ (`hCO`). Let $\varpi\in O$ (`hϖO`), let $c_x,c_y\in O$, let $u$ be a unit of $O$, and let
--   $$\iota\colon \widehat O\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,\widehat A\,(\varpi^m)=\widehat A[\![U,V]\!]/(UV-\varpi^m)$$
--   be a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of $O$ onto the crossing model over the adic completion $\widehat A$ of $A$ with parameter the $m$-th power of the image of $\varpi$, and let $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ be units of that crossing model. Assume $c_xc_y=\varpi^m u$ in $O$ (`hcxy`), that $\iota$ carries the image of each $a\in A$ to `UVCrossingModel.const` of the image of $a$ (`hιc`), that $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\cdot$`UVCrossingModel.U` (`hιx`) and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\cdot$`UVCrossingModel.V` (`hιy`), that $c_y$, if it lies in $W$, lies in $\mathfrak m_W$ (`hcyW`), and that $c_x$, if it lies in $W$, does not lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ (`hcxW`).
--
--   Conclusion. There exists $b\in C$ such that $b\in y$ and the image of $b$ in the adic completion of $O$, transported by $\iota$, does not lie in the ideal of the crossing model generated by `UVCrossingModel.U` and `UVCrossingModel.const` of the image of $\varpi$ in $\widehat A$.
--
--   At an end of the blow-up of the supersingular point of the rigid-level chart, the completed local ring is a crossing $\widehat A[\![U,V]\!]/(UV-\varpi^m)$ with the $V$-branch the exceptional direction; the statement produces an element of the supersingular maximal ideal $y$ whose image avoids the ideal $(U,\varpi)$, which identifies the $U$-branch as the strict transform of the Igusa component rather than the exceptional curve. It is used in the construction of the Igusa branch as a valuation subring in the auxiliary level-one frame, where the auxiliary full level is replaced by the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-type condition $\gamma_{11}\equiv1\pmod\ell$ for a prime $\ell\equiv11\pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, so that no lower bound on $q$ is required.
